CONCLUSION
The College Hostel Management & Maintenance System provides an organized and efficient database solution for managing the major activities of a college hostel. It brings together essential information related to students, hostels, rooms, room allocations, staff, attendance, fees, complaints and maintenance operations.
The database design uses appropriate entities, relationships, primary keys, foreign keys and integrity constraints to maintain data consistency and reduce redundancy. The room-sharing allocation model allows multiple students to share a room while keeping track of their individual allocation details. The system also supports hostel administration by providing a structured way to manage student records, monitor fee payments, record attendance, handle complaints and track maintenance activities.
Overall, the project demonstrates the practical application of DBMS concepts in developing a reliable, organized and maintainable hostel management system. It simplifies record management, improves data accuracy and provides a foundation for efficient hostel administration.


